module

public import Mathlib.AlgebraicGeometry.Modules.Tilde
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.NonvanishingTrivialization.Basic
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.QuasiAffineNonvanishing.Basic

/-!
# An invertible module on an affine spectrum is generated by its global sections

Let `A` be a commutative ring and `L` an invertible module on `Spec A`. Then every point of
`Spec A` lies in the nonvanishing locus of a *global* section of `L`. This is the global
generation input that `StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/QuasiAffineNonvanishing/Basic.lean`
leaves as the hypothesis `hgen` of its form of [Stacks, Tag 0F20], and supplying it here makes
the two inclusions of Tag 0F20 unconditional on an affine spectrum.

## The argument

An invertible module has, near every point, a local section whose germ escapes `𝔪_x L_x`
(`Stacks.SheafOfModules.exists_notMem_maximalIdeal_smul_top_of_isInvertible`). What is missing
is to replace that local section by a global one, and that is exactly where quasi-coherence
enters: an invertible module is quasi-coherent
(`Stacks.SheafOfModules.Scheme.isQuasicoherent_of_isInvertible`, Tag 01BD), a quasi-coherent
module on `Spec A` is the module associated to its global sections
(Mathlib's `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules.isIso_fromTildeΓ_of_isQuasicoherent`), and an
associated module *localizes* on standard opens
(`AlgebraicGeometry.isIso_fromTildeΓ_iff_isLocalizing`). So on a standard open `D(g)` inside the
chosen neighbourhood, the local section becomes `g^{-n}` times the restriction of a global
section `m`, and since `g` is invertible in the local ring at a point of `D(g)` the germ of `m`
there escapes `𝔪_x L_x` as well.

This is Stacks' alternative to the direct argument from exactness of global sections on
quasi-coherent modules ([Stacks, Tag 01IB]), which is not in the library.

## Main results

* `Stacks.SheafOfModules.exists_restrict_eq_smul_of_isQuasicoherent`: the extension step. For a
  quasi-coherent module on `Spec A` and a section over a standard open `D(g)`, some power of `g`
  times that section is the restriction of a global section.
* `Stacks.SheafOfModules.notMem_maximalIdeal_smul_top_of_restrict_eq_smul`: the germ step, on an
  arbitrary ringed space. If a global section restricts, on some neighbourhood of `x`, to a
  function with invertible germ times a section whose germ escapes `𝔪_x L_x`, then its own germ
  escapes `𝔪_x L_x`.
* `Stacks.SheafOfModules.exists_mem_nonvanishingLocus_of_spec`: **global generation of an
  invertible module on `Spec A`.** Every point lies in the nonvanishing locus of a global
  section.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules.exists_sections_finite_subset_nonvanishingOpen_of_spec`:
  clauses 2 and 3 of [Stacks, Tag 0F20] on `Spec A`, with no hypothesis beyond invertibility.

## Implementation notes

The extension step is stated with the standard open presented as an abstract `U : (Spec A).Opens`
together with `hU : U = PrimeSpectrum.basicOpen g`, rather than as `PrimeSpectrum.basicOpen g`
itself. The reason is that `PrimeSpectrum.basicOpen g` has type `Opens (PrimeSpectrum A)` while
the scalar actions on sections are indexed by `(Spec A).Opens`; the two types are definitionally
equal but not interchangeable during instance search, so a statement spelled with
`PrimeSpectrum.basicOpen g` cannot find `Module A Γ(L, D(g))`. With `U` abstract every instance
is found at elaboration time, and `hU` is substituted only inside the proof, where the single
step that needs it is transporting Mathlib's `IsLocalizing`.

For the same reason the germ step is factored out as a statement about a bare ringed space: the
germ lemmas take their open as an `Opens X.carrier`, and keeping `Spec` out of that statement
avoids the mismatch entirely.

Two `rw`s on the nonvanishing locus were replaced by `Eq.trans`/`congrArg` terms and by `.mpr`
applied directly, because `Stacks.SheafOfModules.nonvanishingLocus` is indexed by
`SheafOfModules (structureSheafRing X)` whereas `L : (Spec A).Modules` is indexed by
`(Spec A).ringCatSheaf`; the two agree by `rfl` but `rw`'s `kabstract` will not see through it.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0F20](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0F20)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01IB](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01IB)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01CY](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01CY)
-/

@[expose] public section

open AlgebraicGeometry CategoryTheory Opposite TopologicalSpace
open Stacks.SheafOfModules.TensorStalkRingedSpace

universe u

namespace Stacks.SheafOfModules

/-- **The extension step.** Let `L` be a quasi-coherent module on `Spec A` and let `a` be a
section of `L` over the standard open `D(g)`. Then `g ^ n • a` is the restriction of a global
section of `L`, for some `n`. This is Mathlib's `IsLocalizing` — sections of a quasi-coherent
module localize on standard opens — read in the form the germ computation consumes. -/
theorem exists_restrict_eq_smul_of_isQuasicoherent {A : CommRingCat.{u}} (L : (Spec A).Modules)
    [L.IsQuasicoherent] (g : A) (U : (Spec A).Opens) (hU : U = PrimeSpectrum.basicOpen g)
    (a : Γ(L, U)) :
    ∃ (m : Γ(L, (⊤ : (Spec A).Opens))) (n : ℕ),
      L.presheaf.map U.leTop.op m =
        ((Spec A).presheaf.map U.leTop.op ((Scheme.ΓSpecIso A).inv (g ^ n))) • a := by
  have hIso : IsIso (Scheme.Modules.fromTildeΓ L) :=
    Scheme.Modules.isIso_fromTildeΓ_of_isQuasicoherent L
  have hloc : IsLocalizedModule (Submonoid.powers g)
      ((modulesSpecToSheaf.obj L).obj.map U.leTop.op).hom := by
    subst hU
    exact (isIso_fromTildeΓ_iff_isLocalizing L).mp hIso g
  obtain ⟨⟨m, s⟩, hms⟩ := IsLocalizedModule.surj (self := hloc) _ _ a
  obtain ⟨n, hn⟩ := s.2
  exact ⟨m, n, Eq.symm (Eq.trans (((Scheme.Modules.smul_Spec_def (g ^ n) a).symm).trans
    (congrArg (fun r : A => r • a) hn)) hms)⟩

/-- **The germ step.** If a global section `m` of `L` restricts, over an open `V` containing `x`,
to `r|_V • a|_V` where the germ of the function `r` at `x` is a unit and the germ of `a` at `x`
escapes `𝔪_x L_x`, then the germ of `m` at `x` escapes `𝔪_x L_x` too. -/
theorem notMem_maximalIdeal_smul_top_of_restrict_eq_smul {X : RingedSpace.{u, u}}
    [∀ x : X.carrier, IsLocalRing (ringStalk X x)]
    (L : _root_.SheafOfModules.{u} (structureSheafRing X)) {V W : Opens X.carrier}
    {x : X.carrier} (hxV : x ∈ V) (hVW : V ≤ W) (a : L.val.obj (op W)) (m : L.val.obj (op ⊤))
    (r : X.presheaf.obj (op ⊤)) (hr : IsUnit (ringGerm X x ⊤ (Opens.mem_top x) r))
    (hm : L.val.map (Opens.leTop V).op m
      = (X.presheaf.map (Opens.leTop V).op r) • L.val.map (homOfLE hVW).op a)
    (ha : grpGerm X L.val x W (hVW hxV) a ∉
      IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (ringStalk X x) •
        (⊤ : Submodule (ringStalk X x) (grpStalk X L.val x))) :
    grpGerm X L.val x ⊤ (Opens.mem_top x) m ∉
      IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (ringStalk X x) •
        (⊤ : Submodule (ringStalk X x) (grpStalk X L.val x)) := by
  have hgerm1 : grpGerm X L.val x V hxV (L.val.map (Opens.leTop V).op m)
      = grpGerm X L.val x ⊤ (Opens.mem_top x) m :=
    TopCat.Presheaf.germ_res_apply (C := AddCommGrpCat.{u}) L.val.presheaf (Opens.leTop V) x hxV m
  have hgerm2 : grpGerm X L.val x V hxV (L.val.map (homOfLE hVW).op a)
      = grpGerm X L.val x W (hVW hxV) a :=
    TopCat.Presheaf.germ_res_apply (C := AddCommGrpCat.{u}) L.val.presheaf (homOfLE hVW) x hxV a
  have hringgerm : ringGerm X x V hxV (X.presheaf.map (Opens.leTop V).op r)
      = ringGerm X x ⊤ (Opens.mem_top x) r :=
    TopCat.Presheaf.germ_res_apply (C := CommRingCat.{u}) X.presheaf (Opens.leTop V) x hxV r
  have hkey : grpGerm X L.val x ⊤ (Opens.mem_top x) m
      = ringGerm X x ⊤ (Opens.mem_top x) r • grpGerm X L.val x W (hVW hxV) a :=
    hgerm1.symm.trans ((congrArg (grpGerm X L.val x V hxV) hm).trans
      ((stalkModule_germ_smul X L.val x V hxV _ _).trans
        ((congrArg (fun z : ringStalk X x => z • grpGerm X L.val x V hxV
            (L.val.map (homOfLE hVW).op a)) hringgerm).trans
          (congrArg (fun z => ringGerm X x ⊤ (Opens.mem_top x) r • z) hgerm2))))
  rw [hkey]
  exact (smul_notMem_maximalIdeal_smul_top_iff _ _).mpr ⟨hr, ha⟩

/-- **An invertible module on `Spec A` is generated by its global sections**, in the sense that
every point lies in the nonvanishing locus of some global section. This is the hypothesis `hgen`
of `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules.exists_sections_finite_subset_nonvanishingOpen`. -/
theorem exists_mem_nonvanishingLocus_of_spec {A : CommRingCat.{u}} (L : (Spec A).Modules)
    [IsInvertible (Spec A).presheaf
      (structureSheafRing (Spec A).toRingedSpace).property L] (y : Spec A) :
    ∃ s : L.sections, y ∈ nonvanishingLocus (X := (Spec A).toRingedSpace) L s := by
  have : L.IsQuasicoherent := Scheme.isQuasicoherent_of_isInvertible (Spec A) L
  obtain ⟨W, hyW, a, ha⟩ :=
    exists_notMem_maximalIdeal_smul_top_of_isInvertible (X := (Spec A).toRingedSpace) L y
  obtain ⟨V, hVmem, hyV, hVW⟩ :=
    Opens.isBasis_iff_nbhd.mp PrimeSpectrum.isBasis_basic_opens hyW
  obtain ⟨g, hg⟩ := hVmem
  obtain ⟨m, n, hmn⟩ := exists_restrict_eq_smul_of_isQuasicoherent L g V hg.symm
    (L.presheaf.map (homOfLE hVW).op a)
  refine ⟨sectionsOfTop (X := (Spec A).toRingedSpace) L m,
    (mem_nonvanishingLocus_sectionsOfTop_iff (X := (Spec A).toRingedSpace) L m y).mpr ?_⟩
  have hunitg : IsUnit (ringGerm (Spec A).toRingedSpace y ⊤ (Opens.mem_top y)
      ((Scheme.ΓSpecIso A).inv g)) := by
    rw [isUnit_ringGerm_iff_mem_basicOpen]
    show y ∈ (Spec A).basicOpen ((Scheme.ΓSpecIso A).inv g)
    rw [basicOpen_eq_of_affine, hg]
    exact hyV
  have hunit : IsUnit (ringGerm (Spec A).toRingedSpace y ⊤ (Opens.mem_top y)
      ((Scheme.ΓSpecIso A).inv (g ^ n))) := by
    rw [map_pow, map_pow]
    exact hunitg.pow n
  exact notMem_maximalIdeal_smul_top_of_restrict_eq_smul (X := (Spec A).toRingedSpace)
    L hyV hVW a m _ hunit hmn ha

end Stacks.SheafOfModules

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules

/-- **Clauses 2 and 3 of Stacks Project, Tag 0F20 on an affine spectrum.** A finite set `E`
inside an open `W` of `Spec A` lies in the nonvanishing locus of a single global section of an
invertible module `L`, and that locus is contained in `W`. The global generation hypothesis of
`exists_sections_finite_subset_nonvanishingOpen` is discharged by
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.exists_mem_nonvanishingLocus_of_spec`.

Clause 1 of Tag 0F20, affineness of the nonvanishing locus, is Tag 01PV. It is not proved here —
it is `Stacks.NonvanishingAffineIntersection.isAffineOpen_inf_nonvanishingOpen` of
`../NonvanishingAffineIntersection/Basic.lean` — and nothing below states it, so the
`@[stacks 0F20]` tag is not placed on this statement; it sits on
`Stacks.Tag0F20.exists_affine_nonvanishingOpen_containing_finite_sections` of
`../QuasiAffineGlobalGeneration/Basic.lean`. -/
theorem exists_sections_finite_subset_nonvanishingOpen_of_spec {A : CommRingCat.{u}}
    (L : (Spec A).Modules)
    [Stacks.SheafOfModules.IsInvertible (Spec A).presheaf
      (structureSheafRing (Spec
        A).toRingedSpace).property L]
    {E : Set (Spec A)} (hE : E.Finite) (W : (Spec A).Opens) (hEW : E ⊆ W) :
    ∃ s : L.sections,
      E ⊆ Stacks.SheafOfModules.nonvanishingOpen (X := (Spec A).toRingedSpace) L s ∧
      Stacks.SheafOfModules.nonvanishingOpen (X := (Spec A).toRingedSpace) L s ≤ W :=
  exists_sections_finite_subset_nonvanishingOpen (Spec A) L
    (fun y => Stacks.SheafOfModules.exists_mem_nonvanishingLocus_of_spec L y) hE W hEW

end AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules

end
